  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "The two DS1522+ A26 tables are registered and have the specified masks.",
      "result": "confirmed",
      "evidence": "OEM raw offsets 0x23a8 and 0x3d30, pointers in table list at 0x5cac and 0x5cb0 respectively. Masks at header+8 are 0x000000ff and 0x3f001f00."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Platform index selects tables via the mask at header+8.",
      "result": "confirmed",
      "evidence": "AmdCpmInitPeim 0x09b47be7 reads byte main_table+0x31; 0x09b47bf2 shifts integer 1 by that index; 0x09b47c13 reads candidate_header+8; 0x09b47c16-1c accepts zero mask or nonzero intersection."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The class-to-platform mapping produces platform 0 or 8 for classification 0x0b or 0x0c with condition word zero.",
      "result": "confirmed conditional",
      "evidence": "A01 raw table at 0x14c8 has records at 0x14d8 (class11, condition0, platform0) and 0x14fb (class12, condition0, platform8). InitPeim 0x09b4791c uses 7-byte records, tests class at table+0x10+7*i and zero word at +0x13, loads platform at +0x15, stores main_table+0x31. Unmatched class defaults to 0. Specific CPU->class is outside this review."
    },
    {
      "claim": "DXIO record start, stride, type, present and device/function bit offsets are as proposed.",
      "result": "confirmed",
      "evidence": "PcieInitPeim 0x09b4df05 passes table+0x14 as port descriptors. 0x09b4da7b multiplies index by 0x194; 0x09b4da84 tests table+i*stride+0x18 ==1; 0x09b4da8e tests +0x20 bit0; 0x09b4daa1 masks +0x21 with 0x1f and 0x09b4daa9 shifts same byte right5. These are record+4, record+12 and record+13. Record+6 is also used in lane-range comparisons; paired raw bytes+6/+7 were retained as lane_bytes. No independent public structure definition for the +7 field was located in this bounded check."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Platform0 DS1522 table lacks active PCIe01.4 and01.5 and has type16 on lane bytes0/0 and1/1.",
      "result": "confirmed raw/default records",
      "evidence": "Active PCIe predicate requires type1 AND present1. The two01.5-looking descriptors are type0 and must not be counted as active. Type16 entries start at file0x2d34 and0x2ec8."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Platform8 DS1522 table includes the actual R1600 network/JMB root functions.",
      "result": "confirmed default records, hardware correspondence inferred",
      "evidence": "ActivePCIe01.4 at file0x4200 has lane bytes1/1; activePCIe01.5 at0x4394 has lane bytes0/0. Existing R1600 topology identifies NIC switch under01.4 andJMB585 under01.5."
    },
    {
      "claim": "DS1525 provides a useful reciprocal comparison.",
      "result": "confirmed raw/default records",
      "evidence": "Its platform0 table has activePCIe01.1..01.6 including lane0..1 at01.6, matching its model.dtb SATA root. Its platform8 table resembles the non-customized alternative, with type16 lane0/1 and no active01.4/.5."
    }
  ],
